SECTION 1 — DEFINITIONS

"Author" means Raghav, the original creator and copyright holder of the
Software.

"You" means any individual or legal entity exercising permissions granted by
this License.

"Personal Use" means use by a natural person for their own private, non-revenue-
generating purposes, including learning, experimentation, and building personal
tools that are not distributed to others or used in a commercial context.

"Non-Commercial Use" means use that is not primarily intended for or directed
toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation. This includes academic
research, student projects, open-source contributions, and personal portfolio
work, provided no revenue is derived from the use of this Software.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software, in whole or in part, that
directly or indirectly generates revenue, supports a product or service that
generates revenue, or is used within a commercial organisation for operational
purposes — regardless of whether the end user pays for the Software itself.

"Derivative Work" means any work that is based on or derived from the Software,
including modifications, translations, adaptations, or any software that
incorporates a substantial portion of the Software's source code or logic.

"Distribution" means making the Software or a Derivative Work available to any
third party by any means, including but not limited to publishing on a public
repository, sharing via file transfer, packaging in an application, or deploying
as a hosted service accessible to others.

